From 4769254ecb4d74aaa4f52db4aa335f724ad5064b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sacha Gavino <sacha.gavino@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 22:32:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Stage 4 Part 1b: precompute the IMOD / ER / ANY
 classification

The type-14 grain-surface loop in set_dependant_rates re-derived, on every RHS
call, a per-reaction classification purely from compound names: the IMOD1/IMOD2
diffusion-modification flags (JH/JH2/JO base, then the MODIFY_RATE_FLAG atom
list), the ANY(J)/ANY(K) "has a surface/mantle compound" tests, the JH2+JH2
encounter-desorption test, and the three Eley-Rideal accretion-correction
patterns. MODIFY_RATE_FLAG and GRAIN_TUNNELING_DIFFUSION are run constants, so
this whole classification is a pure function of (reaction, config) and is now
built once in build_index_maps.

New per-reaction maps: IMOD1_BASE/IMOD2_BASE (feed the tunnelling gate),
IMOD1_FINAL/IMOD2_FINAL (base transformed by the MODIFY_RATE_FLAG block, feed
modify_specific_rates), HAS_SURFACE_COMPOUND, HAS_MANTLE_COMPOUND,
IS_H2H2_SURFACE, and ER_PATTERN. The base->final transition was verified to be
config-only: the tunnelling logic between the two uses reads per-call rates but
never writes IMOD, and modify_specific_rates receives the per-call abundances as
separate arguments, so IMOD collapses fully to lookups. The per-call physics
(tunnelling, activation barrier, modify_specific_rates) is untouched; only the
name classification moved to init. A dead empty JH+JH guard (no body) was
removed. This closes Part 1: no per-call string parse or comparison remains in
the RHS grain path.

Kept as its own commit (separate from Part 1a) because the IMOD base-then-modify
control flow is the subtle part; isolating it keeps a later coagulation bisect
pointed at one focused change.

Verified byte-identical against the Part-1a build. Because the defaults
(grain_tunneling_diffusion=0, modify_rate_flag=0) skip the tunnelling and MODIFY
blocks entirely, verification used configurations that actually exercise them:
  - grain_tunneling_diffusion=3, modify_rate_flag=3, is_er_cir=1  (QM3 tunnelling
    + the atom-list final classification + ER patterns),
  - grain_tunneling_diffusion=1, modify_rate_flag=-1,
  - modify_rate_flag=1,
each confirmed to change the trajectory versus default and each byte-identical
between the two builds; plus the tabulated reference case, a derived 4-bin MRN
case (abundances/elemental/dust_distribution), and tests/roundtrip_derived.sh.
